test_command=sh tests/orchestrator-status-probe_test.sh && sh tests/antz-flow_test.sh
id=probealign-01 result=green reason=unit test "probealign-01: the extraction admits no hyphen in the feature portion (shape [A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*-[0-9]+) and every conforming id extracts exactly as before" (tests/orchestrator-status-probe_test.sh) passes -- scripts/orchestration/antz-probe.sh's id-extraction grep is now grep -oE '[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*-[0-9]+' (the tolerant [A-Za-z0-9_-] class is gone, asserted both ways), the fixture's every reported id matches the convention shape exactly, and the conforming cases extract byte-identically to before: "api-1,api-2" from one sub-spec, "client-1" from another, the multi-line tag's first-line id ("install-01"), a "Scenario Outline:" tag ("outline-1") like a plain tag, and an underscore-carrying feature name ("user_profile-1") whole; the index portion stays one-or-more digits (the single-digit fixture ids still extract, so the probe does not enforce the two-digit padding)
id=probealign-02 result=green reason=unit tests "probealign-02 probe-subspec-ids-hyphenated-feature: a conforming one-word feature name extracts whole while a hyphenated feature name yields only its trailing convention-shaped portion" and "probealign-02: a hyphenated feature tag reports only its trailing convention-shaped portion, surfaces downstream as a foreign-id mismatch, and every other probe output is byte-unchanged" (tests/orchestrator-status-probe_test.sh) pass -- the hyphenated tag "user-profile-1" now reports exactly ids=profile-1 (the pre-change tolerant whole-id report is gone, and the suite no longer pins it anywhere), the rewritten hyphenated-feature test pins both sides (conforming "userprofile-1" whole, violating "user-profile-1" -> "profile-1"), a receipt naming the whole hyphenated id reads as a foreign id (covered=0/1 complete=no class=in_progress, never done) while the convention-following receipt still gives covered=1/1 complete=yes class=done (the mapping unchanged), and open_questions=no/yes, rejected_count=0/1, and the change_dir=missing short-circuit with its non-zero exit are byte-unchanged with the violating fixture present
id=probealign-03 result=green reason=unit test "probealign-03: this suite pins the aligned extraction -- the tolerant pin is rewritten both-sided, the hyphenated-feature fixtures are updated with their properties intact, the assertions carry the probealign ids, and every other assertion stays byte-identical to HEAD" (tests/orchestrator-status-probe_test.sh) passes -- the second-review-mandated test update lands in this same change inside the same self-contained suite: the three probealign ids appear in reported run_test names, the tolerant expectation is gone, the fixtures that carried hyphenated-feature ids are convention-shaped now ("install-01" in the multi-line-tag test, "picker-01" in the tag-crossref test, with the crossref leak check tightened to "cmd-06" so even a violation-splitting leak is caught) while their own properties still run (multi-line pickup, cross-reference non-extraction), and every other assertion's function -- the probe-extracted/testharness-02 guards, the open-questions, rejection-count, ids-extraction, empty-ids, change-dir, and all receipts-06 receipt-field groups -- is byte-identical to HEAD's copy of the file; full regression: all 25 tests/*_test.sh suites green, including tests/antz-flow_test.sh (whose flow-09 scripts byte-unchanged guard this sub-spec's invariant re-scopes off antz-probe.sh onto antz-flow.sh + antz-skills.sh, pinned by ensure-19) and the render guards (tests/orchestrator-render-sync_test.sh, tests/renderinject_test.sh) that keep install.sh's injection of the edited probe byte-synchronous
